Computercraft-Legacy
===================

This distribution is a modified version of ComputerCraft for Minecraft 1.7.10.
It is distributed under the ComputerCraft Public License (CCPL); the full text
is in LICENSE. This file records where the code came from, because that is not
recoverable from the license files alone.


1. Provenance of the ComputerCraft code
---------------------------------------

The ComputerCraft source code for Minecraft 1.7.10 was never published.
Public ComputerCraft source begins with the Minecraft 1.8 line: the oldest
tag in dan200/ComputerCraft is 1.79, which is the Minecraft 1.8.9 build.
No 1.7.10 source tree has been released by the original authors.

The ComputerCraft code in this project was therefore recovered by decompiling
the Minecraft 1.7.10 binary distribution of ComputerCraft 1.75, which was the
last ComputerCraft release for Minecraft 1.7.10. This is corroborated by the
bundled in-game changelog, whose most recent entry is "New Features in
ComputerCraft 1.75"; no later version appears anywhere in the ROM.

That decompilation is expressly permitted by the license under which
ComputerCraft was distributed. CCPL section 0 defines a "User" as anybody
that interacts with the software in one of the following ways, and lists
"decompile" among them. CCPL section 4 states:

    "The user has the right to decompile the source code, look at either
     the decompiled version or the original source code, and to modify it."

All recovered ComputerCraft code, and all ComputerCraft assets, remain
licensed under the CCPL. CCPL section 5 requires this:

    "All distributions of this mod must remain licensed under the CCPL."

Because the ComputerCraft 1.7.10 source was never published, no upstream
file exists to diff against. Provenance of individual files cannot be
established by comparison and is instead recorded by convention: files
carrying no other notice are decompiled ComputerCraft 1.7.10 code under
the CCPL.


2. Code that is not ComputerCraft 1.7.10 code
--------------------------------------------

This project also incorporates code backported from CC: Tweaked
(https://github.com/cc-tweaked/CC-Tweaked), a fork of ComputerCraft
originally maintained by SquidDev and now under the cc-tweaked organisation.
That backport is substantial, and predates the Minecraft
1.7.10 code it is layered onto. In outline it covers:

  - the Cobalt Lua runtime integration, in
    dan200.computercraft.core.lua.lib.cobalt and
    dan200.computercraft.core.lua.binfs
  - the extended Lua API surface in dan200.computercraft.api.lua, which
    includes interfaces that do not exist in ComputerCraft 1.7.10 at all
    (ILuaAPI, IArguments, ArgumentDelegator, IBinaryHandler, ILuaEnvironment,
    IExtendedLuaObject, IExtendedLuaTask, ILuaAPIFactory,
    ILuaObjectWithArguments, IPeripheralWithArguments, MethodResult,
    ILuaCallback)
  - the Lua library and delayed-task runtime in
    dan200.computercraft.core.lua.lib (DelayedTask, DelayedTasks,
    LuaEnvironment, LuaHelpers, BinaryConverter)
  - the computer and peripheral registry architecture in
    dan200.computercraft.shared.computer.core (ComputerRegistry,
    ClientComputerRegistry, ServerComputerRegistry, ComputerFamily,
    TileComputerBase) and its peripherals, which the 1.7.10 code does not
    use, and which coexist in this tree with the 1.7.10-era
    ComputerPeripheral / TileWirelessModem / WirelessModemPeripheral code
  - backported Lua ROM modules under
    assets/computercraft/lua/rom/modules/main/cc, which carry
    SPDX-License-Identifier: MPL-2.0 headers

Files sourced from CC: Tweaked are licensed under the Mozilla Public
License 2.0. The full text is in LICENSE-MPL-2.0. MPL-2.0 is a
file-level copyleft: those files remain MPL-2.0, and only those files.

